{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794232145,"nonce":"/erm4VDqDBSuZ1grAUQXY8Yrp0c=","title":"The code editor builds every line on every change: virtualize it","message":"`CodeEditor` is a `Stateful` whose callback rebuilds the whole content on each\nchange: every unfolded line (`visible_lines()` means unfolded, not on screen),\nits tokens, the gutter row for each, and every selection, diagnostic and\nbracket box. Cost is linear in the document.\n\nMeasured (release, headless, 800x600, a typical 40-column line, line numbers on):\n\n| lines | mount   | one keystroke | layout nodes |\n|-------|---------|---------------|--------------|\n| 100   | 21 ms   | 6 ms          | 615          |\n| 1000  | 192 ms  | 66 ms         | 6015         |\n| 5000  | 1018 ms | 1045 ms       | 30015        |\n\nashui's CodeEditor (components/haxe/ashui/components/CodeEditor.hx), which\nRayDE uses, is bounded by the viewport instead. Its model, to port:\n\n- Row window. `firstRow`/`endRow` are signals set from the scroll offset with\n  three rows of overscan either side, and set only when they change, so a\n  scroll inside the window runs nothing.\n- Slot pool. A fixed number of row slots (viewport rows + 9, grown, never\n  shrunk below the window). Row r lives in slot r % capacity; each slot is a\n  persistent element whose row is a signal. A scroll re-points the slots\n  whose row changed; nothing is built. Slots with no row are hidden, not\n  faded (a group at zero opacity is still drawn).\n- Token pool. Each slot keeps token elements pooled by kind, grows them on\n  demand and trims when use falls under a quarter.\n- Horizontal window. Text is clipped to 256 px buckets around the view with\n  one bucket of overscan, so a 10,000 px line submits only what is near the\n  screen, and a small pan reuses its tokens. Clipping respects shaped\n  clusters and reordered (bidi) text.\n- Row cache. A row is rebuilt only when its line, token revision, top or\n  horizontal window changed.\n- Everything per row (selection, decorations, search marks, brackets) is\n  computed over the window's rows, not the document.\n- Content height and width are computed (widest column from metrics), so\n  the scroll extent is right without laying out every line.\n\nashui's test fixture `tests/fixtures/components/CodeViewportCulling.hx`\npins the contract: rows bounded by the viewport, runs bounded by horizontal\noverscan, sub-line scrolling rebuilds nothing, caret geometry is exact off\nscreen, and a pan does not anchor text at the line origin. Port it as a\nrecorder test.\n\nThis is also the move off `Stateful` for the editor (signals and bound\nproperties; the 0.6 direction), so the horizontal scroll added for the\nrussl toy (`scroll_x`, cross-axis wheel to the container's handler) should\nbecome the scroll container's x offset feeding the horizontal window.","files":null}]}